+# Plugin Marketplace — Contract
+
+## 1. Plugin Registry (`src/registry.ts`)
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 1.1 | `register(manifest)` inserts a plugin manifest; storing it in the database | Call `register()`, then `get()` returns it |
+| 1.2 | `get(name)` returns the latest version of the plugin with that name, or `null` if not found | Register two versions of same plugin, call `get()` — returns the higher version |
+| 1.3 | `getVersion(name, version)` returns the specific version or `null` | `getVersion("pkg", "1.0.0")` returns that exact version |
+| 1.4 | `list()` returns all plugins (all versions as separate entries) | After registering 2 plugins (2 versions each), `list()` returns 4 entries |
+| 1.5 | `search(query)` matches against name or description (case-insensitive partial match) | Register "HelloWorld", `search("hello")` returns it; `search("world")` returns it; `search("xyz")` returns empty |
+| 1.6 | `remove(name, version)` removes a specific version; returns `true` if removed, `false` if not found | `remove("pkg", "1.0.0")` succeeds; calling again returns `false` |
+| 1.7 | `listVersions(name)` returns all registered version strings for a plugin, sorted descending (newest first) | Register 1.0.0 then 2.0.0, `listVersions` returns `["2.0.0", "1.0.0"]` |
+| 1.8 | `update(name, version, updates)` merges partial updates into an existing manifest | `update("pkg", "1.0.0", { description: "new" })` updates only that field |
+| 1.9 | Multiple versions of same plugin can coexist | Register 1.0.0 and 2.0.0 of "pkg"; both appear in `list()` and `listVersions()` |
+| 1.10 | Operations on nonexistent plugin return null/false gracefully | `get("nonexistent")` → null, `remove("nonexistent", "1.0.0")` → false |
+
+## 2. Version Resolver (`src/resolver.ts`)
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 2.1 | `validRange(range)` returns true if range is valid semver range, false otherwise | `^1.0.0` → true, `abc` → false |
+| 2.2 | `satisfies(version, range)` checks if a version satisfies a semver range | `satisfies("1.2.0", "^1.0.0")` → true; `satisfies("2.0.0", "^1.0.0")` → false |
+| 2.3 | `maxSatisfying(versions, range)` returns the newest version satisfying the range | `maxSatisfying(["1.0.0","1.5.0","2.0.0"], "^1.0.0")` → "1.5.0" |
+| 2.4 | `maxSatisfying` returns null when no versions satisfy the range | `maxSatisfying(["2.0.0"], "^1.0.0")` → null |
+| 2.5 | `resolve(constraints, available)` takes constraints and available versions, returns ResolvedVersion[] | resolve `[{name:"a",range:"^1.0.0"},{name:"b",range:"~2.0.0"}]` with `{a:["1.0.0","1.5.0"],b:["2.0.0","2.1.0"]}` returns proper ResolvedVersion objects |
+| 2.6 | `resolve` returns empty array for empty constraints | `resolve([], {})` → `[]` |
+| 2.7 | `resolve` omits constraints that cannot be satisfied (graceful) | If no version of "a" satisfies "^3.0.0", that constraint is omitted from result |
+
+## 3. Sandboxed Runner (`src/runner.ts`)
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 3.1 | `execute(code)` runs JS code in vm sandbox, returns SandboxResult with success=true | `execute("1+1")` → `{success:true, output:2, ...}` |
+| 3.2 | `execute(code, context)` passes context variables into the sandbox | `execute("a+b", {a:1,b:2})` → output 3 |
+| 3.3 | Code that throws returns `success:false` with error message | `execute("throw new Error('bad')")` → `{success:false, error:"bad"}` |
+| 3.4 | `executeWithTimeout(code, timeoutMs)` enforces timeout; code exceeding it returns `success:false` with timeout error | `executeWithTimeout("while(true){}", 100)` → `{success:false, error:"Timeout"}` |
+| 3.5 | Duration is measured in milliseconds (number) | `execute("1+1")` returns `duration` as a positive number |
+| 3.6 | `memoryUsed` is a number (from `process.memoryUsage()`) | `execute("1+1")` returns `memoryUsed` as a positive number |
+| 3.7 | Sandbox does not have access to Node.js globals (require, process, module) | `execute("typeof require")` → output `"undefined"`; `execute("typeof process")` → output `"undefined"` |
+
+## 4. Review System (`src/review.ts`)
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 4.1 | `addReview(review)` creates a review with auto-generated id, createdAt, flagged=false; returns the full Review | `addReview({pluginName:"pkg",pluginVersion:"1.0.0",userId:"user1",rating:4,comment:"good"})` returns Review with id, createdAt, flagged=false |
+| 4.2 | `getReviews(pluginName)` returns all non-flagged reviews for a plugin | Add 2 non-flagged + 1 flagged review for "pkg"; `getReviews("pkg")` returns 2 entries |
+| 4.3 | `getAverageRating(pluginName)` returns average (0-5) excluding flagged reviews | For plugin with ratings [5,4,1] where 1 is flagged, avg = (5+4)/2 = 4.5 |
+| 4.4 | `getAverageRating` returns 0 when no non-flagged reviews exist | `getAverageRating("empty")` → 0 |
+| 4.5 | `flagReview(reviewId)` marks a review as flagged | After `flagReview(1)`, that review appears in `getFlaggedReviews()` |
+| 4.6 | `getFlaggedReviews()` returns all flagged reviews | Returns only reviews where flagged=true |
+| 4.7 | `removeReview(reviewId)` deletes a review; returns true/false | `removeReview(1)` → true; calling again → false |
+| 4.8 | `getReviewsByUser(userId)` returns all reviews by a user | User "u1" left 2 reviews; `getReviewsByUser("u1")` returns 2 |
+| 4.9 | `getReviewCount(pluginName)` returns count of non-flagged reviews | For plugin with 3 non-flagged + 1 flagged, count = 3 |
+| 4.10 | Duplicate reviews (same user+plugin+version) should be rejected (returns null or throws) | `addReview` for same user/plugin/version twice → second returns null |
+
+## 5. Dependency Graph (`src/deps.ts`)
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 5.1 | `buildTree(name, registry)` builds a DependencyNode tree from the registry | For plugin "A" depending on "B" depending on "C", returns tree A→B→C |
+| 5.2 | `buildTree` leaf nodes have empty `dependencies` array | Plugin with no deps returns `{dependencies:[]}` |
+| 5.3 | `detectCycles(name, registry)` returns `null` if no cycles | A→B→C with no cycles returns null |
+| 5.4 | `detectCycles(name, registry)` returns `string[][]` listing cycles when cycles exist | A→B→A returns `[["A","B","A"]]` |
+| 5.5 | `hasCircularDependency(name, registry)` returns boolean | `true` when cycle exists, `false` otherwise |
+| 5.6 | `topologicalSort(name, registry)` returns ordered list with dependencies before dependents | A→B→C → `["C","B","A"]` (deps first) |
+| 5.7 | `topologicalSort` throws on circular dependency | A→B→A → throws Error |
+| 5.8 | `flattenDependencies(name, registry)` returns all transitive dependency names (unique) | A→B, A→C, B→D → `["B","C","D"]` (order doesn't matter for unique) |
+
+## 6. Integration Layer (`src/index.ts`)
+
+| # | Behavior | Verification |
+|---|----------|-------------|
+| 6.1 | `createMarketplace()` returns an object with all 5 services | Result has properties: registry, resolver, runner, reviews, deps + installPlugin |
+| 6.2 | `installPlugin(manifest)` returns `{resolved: ResolvedVersion[], result: SandboxResult}` | Returns correct shape |
+| 6.3 | `installPlugin` validates required fields (name, version, entryPoint) — throws if missing | `installPlugin({version:"1.0.0",entryPoint:"index.js",...})` without name → throws |
+| 6.4 | `installPlugin` registers the plugin in the registry | After `installPlugin`, `registry.get(name)` returns it |
+| 6.5 | `installPlugin` resolves dependency versions using resolver | Plugin with deps `{a:"^1.0.0"}` gets them resolved |
+| 6.6 | `installPlugin` checks for circular dependencies and rejects if found | If dep chain has cycle, `installPlugin` throws |
+| 6.7 | `installPlugin` executes the entryPoint in the sandbox | EntryPoint code runs and result is returned |
+| 6.8 | Dependency registration happens before execution | Dependencies available for the sandbox execution context |
